<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation 1027</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2023">2023</a>–<a href="/years/2024">2024</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myanmar-civil-war-2021-present">Myanmar civil war (2021–present)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation 1027 was an offensive launched on 27 October 2023 by the Three Brotherhood Alliance of ethnic armed groups in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shan-state">Shan State</a>, Myanmar. It captured towns, military posts and border crossings with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, including Laukkai, and was the military junta's greatest defeat since the coup of 2021, encouraging resistance offensives elsewhere in the country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-1027.jpg" alt="Operation 1027" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clyde H. Mapping · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Operation_1027.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
